cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OpenCEA in academic or applied work, please cite it as below."
title: "OpenCEA: Open, reproducible health-economic decision modeling in Python"
abstract: >-
  OpenCEA is a Python library for cohort state-transition cost-effectiveness
  analysis. Its deterministic engine reproduces the peer-reviewed DARTH
  Sick-Sicker reference model to the cent and to the dollar. It provides
  vectorized probabilistic sensitivity analysis with CEAC and frontier,
  one-way deterministic sensitivity analysis with tornado, and an applied
  empagliflozin case study.
type: software
authors:
